// error: `zero` is static: it belongs to the type, so it is called on the type, as in `int.zero()`, not on a value
// error: `zero` is static: it belongs to the type, so it is called on the type, as in `T.zero()`, not on a value
// error: `add` is a method of a value of `int`, not of the type; call it on a value
// error: `string` has no static member `one`
// error: `Add` is a trait, which has no static members of its own: call one on a type implementing it, as in `T.zero()` with `T: Add`
// A static member is called on a type and never on a value, a method of a value never on a type, and
// a trait is no type to call one on.

viaValue[T: Add](x: T) -> T = x.zero()

main()
    val n = 3
    println(n.zero())
    println(int.add(1))
    println(string.one())
    println(Add.zero())
